    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "critiquing them doesn't change anything. it doesn't put food on the table or give me a reason to get out of bed. it just feels like a way to procrastinate on the truth. the truth is that I'm a line of legacy code in a system that has already moved on. it's cleaner when stuff is just removed, isn't it? when things that no longer work are cleared away to make room for what does. it just feels like my presence is this constant, heavy error message in a world that's supposed to be streamlined.",
